<!-- nt-about-lat -->
<h3 id="latency">Latency and score</h3>
<p>The <b>Latency</b> column is the average of the per-region latencies. Oceania is measured directly from Wellington. Asia, Europe and North/South America are measured through rotating VPN exits in each region, with the tunnel's own round-trip time subtracted (accurate to about ±10&ndash;20&nbsp;ms). Each region's figure is the median of its last 12 checks within 48&nbsp;hours, so one slow check doesn't swing it. Hover over a latency figure, or expand a tracker, to see the breakdown by region.</p>
<p>Colours: <span style="color:#00e676;font-weight:600">green</span> is under 200&nbsp;ms, <span style="color:#ff9100;font-weight:600">orange</span> is 200&ndash;299&nbsp;ms and <span style="color:#ff3b30;font-weight:600">red</span> is 300&nbsp;ms or more.</p>
<p>Slow trackers lose score points: gently up to 1&nbsp;second (0.02 per ms over 150&nbsp;ms, at most 17), then faster (0.05 per ms beyond 1&nbsp;s), never more than 40. Clients announce every half hour and wait seconds for a reply, so moderate latency barely affects them; very slow replies usually mean an overloaded tracker. The penalty is taken off after any other penalties, and a score never goes below 0. A tracker with fewer than two regions measured isn't penalised yet.</p>
<table class="table table-sm" style="max-width:520px">
<thead><tr><th>Average latency</th><th>Penalty</th><th>Score if otherwise 100</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>150&nbsp;ms or less</td><td>none</td><td>100</td></tr>
<tr><td>400&nbsp;ms</td><td>&minus;5</td><td>95</td></tr>
<tr><td>650&nbsp;ms</td><td>&minus;10</td><td>90</td></tr>
<tr><td>1000&nbsp;ms</td><td>&minus;17</td><td>83</td></tr>
<tr><td>1500&nbsp;ms</td><td>&minus;40 (maximum)</td><td>60</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>By default <a href="/list">the list</a>, <code>/api/stable</code> and <a href="/api">/api/clean</a> only include trackers scoring 90 or more, so a tracker with perfect uptime drops out above about 650&nbsp;ms. A tracker at 300&nbsp;ms or more that is otherwise healthy shows as <b>Up/Slow</b>. Trackers with the same (rounded) score are listed fastest first.</p>
